[0.45, "o", "Title:      \u001b[1mEnable Guest VM Outbound Networking\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:     \u001b[1m\u001b[92mverified\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\r\nArchetype:  \u001b[95m\u001b[1mStrategic\u001b[0m\u001b[39m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-01\u001b[0m - Guest outbound networking: Attach a TAP/virtio-net interface to Firecracker VMs with host-side NAT so the guest can reach the internet. Flux can clone from GitHub, containerd can pull external images, CoreDNS can resolve. (\u001b[2mVFSWpHXG1\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-02\u001b[0m - Guest DNS resolution: Configure `/etc/resolv.conf` in the guest image with working upstream nameservers (host-forwarded or public). CoreDNS upstream resolution works, K3s service DNS chain is healthy. (\u001b[2m`flux get sources git` shows all GitRepositories as `Ready: True`\u001b[0m)\r\n  \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mMG-03\u001b[0m - Configurable service forwards: Allow operators to declare additional host\u2192guest port forwards beyond the API (6443) so workstation tools can reach cluster services like MinIO console, Envoy preview proxy, and Prometheus. (\u001b[2m`infra health --env local --scene` shows 18/18 OPERATIONAL\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mChildren\u001b[0m\r\n  Epics (1):\r\n    \u001b[1m\u001b[36mVFSWpHXG1\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - Guest VM Outbound Networking (\u001b[2mdone\u001b[0m)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mLatest Log Entry\u001b[0m\r\n    2026-03-31T08:07:08\r\n"]
[1.8, "o", "$ sed -n '1,120p' .keel/missions/VFSRShGlI/CHARTER.md\r\n"]
[2.25, "o", "# Enable Guest VM Outbound Networking - Charter\r\n\r\nArchetype: Strategic\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nPort-managed Firecracker VMs currently have no network interface. The only host-guest communication channel is vsock (used for the API forward on :6443 and guest-agent control). This means K3s CoreDNS cannot resolve external hostnames, Flux cannot clone GitRepository sources from GitHub, containerd cannot pull images from external registries, and any workload requiring outbound HTTP/HTTPS fails. This blocks the entire Flux GitOps reconciliation loop in spoke-sh/infra \u2014 the cluster is stuck at its bootstrap state with 5/18 components permanently degraded.\r\n\r\n## Goals\r\n\r\n| ID | Description | Verification |\r\n|----|-------------|--------------|\r\n| MG-01 | Guest outbound networking: Attach a TAP/virtio-net interface to Firecracker VMs with host-side NAT so the guest can reach the internet. Flux can clone from GitHub, containerd can pull external images, CoreDNS can resolve. | board: VFSWpHXG1 |\r\n| MG-02 | Guest DNS resolution: Configure `/etc/resolv.conf` in the guest image with working upstream nameservers (host-forwarded or public). CoreDNS upstream resolution works, K3s service DNS chain is healthy. | manual: `flux get sources git` shows all GitRepositories as `Ready: True` |\r\n| MG-03 | Configurable service forwards: Allow operators to declare additional host\u2192guest port forwards beyond the API (6443) so workstation tools can reach cluster services like MinIO console, Envoy preview proxy, and Prometheus. | manual: `infra health --env local --scene` shows 18/18 OPERATIONAL |\r\n\r\n## What Needs to Change in Port\r\n\r\n| Area | Current State | Required Change |\r\n|------|---------------|-----------------|\r\n| FirecrackerConfig struct (`port-runtime/src/lib.rs`) | No `network_interfaces` field | Add network interface config (TAP device \u2192 guest eth0) |\r\n| MachineSpec model (`port-model/src/lib.rs`) | No network configuration fields | Add network policy/config to the machine model |\r\n| Guest image build (`scripts/artifacts/build-guest-image.sh`) | No `/etc/resolv.conf`, no network interface setup | Add DNS config, ensure guest init brings up eth0 via DHCP or static config |\r\n| Host-side setup | No TAP device creation, no NAT rules | Create TAP device, configure iptables MASQUERADE for guest subnet |\r\n| Guest kernel/initrd | Loads `virtio_mmio` but no net modules explicitly | Ensure virtio-net and network stack modules are available |\r\n| Forward config | Single hardcoded API forward | Allow operator-declared forwards in `port.toml` or machine spec |\r\n\r\n## Constraints\r\n\r\n- The vsock channel must remain the primary control plane \u2014 networking is for data-plane traffic only.\r\n- Guest networking should be opt-in or default-on for local clusters, but the machine model must support disabling it.\r\n- NAT is sufficient for the local single-node case. Bridged or routed networking can remain follow-on.\r\n- No changes to the existing API forward mechanism \u2014 it works and should stay as-is.\r\n\r\n## Halting Rules\r\n\r\n- DO NOT halt while Flux GitOps reconciliation remains blocked on missing guest outbound networking or DNS resolution.\r\n- HALT when `kubectl exec` into a pod can `wget https://github.com`, `flux get sources git` shows all GitRepositories as `Ready: True`, and `infra health --env local --scene` shows 18/18 OPERATIONAL.\r\n- YIELD to human when the remaining blocker requires a product decision on network topology (bridged vs routed), security policy for guest egress, or non-local scope expansion rather than implementation work.\r\n"]
[3.6, "o", "$ keel epic show VFSWpHXG1\r\n"]
[4.05, "o", "Title:     \u001b[1mGuest VM Outbound Networking\u001b[0m\r\nStatus:    \u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m\r\nCreated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-31 08:27:36\u001b[0m\r\nStarted:   \u001b[2m2026-03-31 10:04:58\u001b[0m\r\nUpdated:   \u001b[2m2026-03-31 10:06:07\u001b[0m\r\nCompleted: \u001b[2m2026-03-31 10:06:07\u001b[0m (\u001b[2m1m\u001b[0m)\r\nPath:      \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFSWpHXG1/README.md\u001b[0m\r\nPRD:       \u001b[2m/home/alex/workspace/spoke-sh/port/.keel/epics/VFSWpHXG1/PRD.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mProblem\u001b[0m\r\n  Firecracker VMs have no network interface \u2014 only vsock exists. This blocks CoreDNS resolution, Flux GitRepository cloning, containerd image pulls, and all outbound HTTP/HTTPS workloads, leaving the Flux GitOps loop in spoke-sh/infra stuck at 5/18 components.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mGoals\u001b[0m\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m: Attach a TAP/virtio-net interface to Firecracker VMs with host-side NAT so the guest can reach the internet. (Pod inside the guest VM can resolve DNS and reach external HTTPS endpoints -> \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl exec\u001b[0m into a pod and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mwget https://github.com\u001b[0m succeeds)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m: Configure working DNS resolution inside the guest image. (CoreDNS upstream resolution works, K3s service DNS chain is healthy -> \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mflux get sources git\u001b[0m shows all GitRepositories as \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mReady: True\u001b[0m)\r\n  - \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m: Allow operators to declare additional host\u2192guest port forwards beyond the API (6443). (Workstation tools can reach cluster services without manual \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl port-forward\u001b[0m -> Declared forwards in \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mport.toml\u001b[0m or machine spec are reachable from the host)\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mScope Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(no scope drift detected)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mStructural Drift\u001b[0m\r\n  Coefficient: 0.63 (severe)\r\n  Coverage:    entities 302/302 | knowledge 5/43 | source 0/0 | docs 0/17\r\n  Context:     38 knowledge units lack source provenance; 17 project docs are unlinked\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mRequirement Coverage\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-01\u001b[39m - Firecracker VM configuration must include a \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mnetwork_interfaces\u001b[0m field that attaches a TAP device as the guest's virtio-net eth0.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-01\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-02\u001b[39m - Port must create and configure a host-side TAP device before VM boot and set up iptables MASQUERADE for the guest subnet.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-03\u001b[39m - The guest image must include a working \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61m/etc/resolv.conf\u001b[0m pointing to reachable upstream nameservers.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-02\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-04\u001b[39m - The guest init must bring up eth0 with an IP address (static or DHCP) on boot.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-04\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-05\u001b[39m - The guest kernel/initrd must include virtio-net and network stack modules.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-05\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-06\u001b[39m - MachineSpec must include network configuration fields to enable/disable guest networking.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-06\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mFR-07\u001b[39m - Operators must be able to declare additional host\u2192guest port forwards beyond the API (6443) in port.toml or machine spec.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-07\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-01\u001b[39m - The vsock channel must remain the primary control plane \u2014 networking is for data-plane traffic only.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-03\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-02\u001b[39m - Guest networking must be opt-in or default-on for local clusters, with the machine model supporting disable.\r\n    Linked goals (1): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-02\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[36mNFR-03\u001b[39m - No changes to the existing API forward mechanism.\r\n    Linked goals (2): \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-01\u001b[0m, \u001b[38;2;255;244;214;48;2;112;80;0;1mGOAL-03\u001b[0m\r\n    Linked children (1): \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m/\u001b[36mSRS-NFR-01\u001b[39m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mPress Release\u001b[0m\r\n  Status:     \u001b[2mnot authored\u001b[0m\r\n  Guidance:   optional; use for large user-facing value shifts\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mProgress\u001b[0m\r\n  Voyages:              1/1 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m1/1\u001b[39m\r\n  Stories:              3/3 \u001b[32m\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u001b[39m \u001b[32m3/3\u001b[39m\r\n  ETA:                  complete\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Strategy\u001b[0m\r\n  Techniques:\r\n    - Area: Method\r\n    - DNS resolution: \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mflux get sources git\u001b[0m shows all GitRepositories as \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mReady: True\u001b[0m\r\n    - Full GitOps reconciliation: \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61minfra health --env local --scene\u001b[0m shows 18/18 OPERATIONAL\r\n    - Guest outbound networking: \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mkubectl exec\u001b[0m into a pod and \u001b[38;2;230;237;243;48;2;48;54;61mwget https://github.com\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVerification Readiness\u001b[0m\r\n  Criteria:              automated 0 | manual 10\r\n  Requirement coverage:  automated 0 | manual 10\r\n  Artifact inventory:    text 0 | media 0 | other 0\r\n\r\n\u001b[1mVoyages\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[35mVFSXWpO18\u001b[39m\u001b[0m - TAP Networking and Host NAT for Local Firecracker VMs (\u001b[32mdone\u001b[39m)\r\n"]
